# Line endings.
#
# Without this, every Windows tool that touches a .bat file rewrites all its
# line endings, and git reports the whole file as changed — 92 insertions and
# 92 deletions in gradlew.bat with not one character of content different.
# That noise buries the real diff, which is the only thing worth reviewing.
#
# So: normalise to LF in the repository, and check out the files that Windows
# genuinely needs as CRLF. A .bat file with LF endings can fail outright on
# older cmd.exe, so this is correctness, not tidiness.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.apk   binary
*.aab   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ico   binary
